+# Verified remote problem data
+
+This optional mode uses the normal grading code with an additional verified
+preparation step. No problem init.yml changes are required. Local clients can
+keep their existing configuration and protocol.
+
+Launch judge processes with `--no-watchdog` in both local and remote deployments.
+Shared-filesystem deployments use the external-storage notifier's private
+`POST /update/problems` calls for inventory refresh. Isolated setups without a
+notifier must call that API explicitly. Remote caches are prepared per run and
+do not rely on watching the VDS filesystem. Do not add `--skip-first-scan` by
+default; disabling watchdog does not disable startup or explicit API scans.
+
+Configure a writable persistent `remote_data_cache` directory to advertise the
+`problem-data-manifest-v1` capability. `remote_data_timeout` defaults to 1800
+seconds. `remote_data_allow_http` defaults to false and exists only for isolated
+development fixtures. Use HTTPS for the OJ data endpoint and R2 downloads, and
+TLS or a private/VPN network for the authenticated judge bridge.
+
+OJ must explicitly classify the client as remote and supply the expected root
+ID, manifest SHA-256 and submission-scoped signed download ticket. The worker
+cannot use stale cache when preparing the requested version fails. It ACKs
+immediately, downloads/verifies in the worker, and handles cancellation during
+preparation. Preparation time is outside contestant execution time.
+
+Cache layout is `<cache>/<root-id>/current/{state.json,data/}` with a stable
+`data.lock` outside the current folder. The state and dataset are published as
+one directory under exclusive flock. Every grader/checker/generator root lookup
+uses the pinned `data/` folder while shared flock is retained through cleanup.
+The requested hash is checked again after acquiring SH; EX-to-SH is not atomic.
+All processes sharing this cache must use this implementation; do not modify
+cache files while workers are running.
+
+Unchanged files are reused after verification; modified archives are downloaded
+whole. Warm identical versions require no network or full hash pass. After a
+controller restart, persisted bytes are reverified once per root before reuse.
+Incomplete staging data is never graded. Abandoned `.staging-*` directories can
+be removed with all cache users stopped. Size disk capacity for current plus
+staging data; there is no automatic cache eviction in this first version.
+
+Download endpoints in the current external-storage service select latest READY.
+The worker verifies against OJ's expected manifest even if that storage snapshot
+changes mid-download. A mismatch sends `problem-data-unavailable` and the OJ
+requeues the run with a fresh dispatch token. A completed preparation sends
+`problem-data-prepared`; normal compile/grading packets follow. An AB run is not
+resurrected by delayed failure or result packets.
+
+Use the same compiler/runtime and built-in checker image configuration as the
+local judges. The manifest covers problem-controlled files, not system packages.
